  (tags "LoRa LR2021 NiceRF F33 castellated PA 2W vendor-land-pattern")
  ;; ================================================================
  ;; GENERATED FILE - do not hand-edit.
  ;;   python3 scripts/gen_f33_landpattern.py
  ;; Pad CENTRES decoded from the VENDOR land file
  ;;   docs/f33-module/materials/LORA2021F33-2G4 footprint_pads.pcb
  ;;   sha256 c66ea27c4409a3af58f1bfd967cddec60214d446d4b15f620f2eef82e86ee7ac
  ;;   (18 x 36-byte records, tag 0x08435AD8, 1.5e6 units/mm)
  ;; Verified against the vendor file and the datasheet drawing:
  ;;   pad count 18, names 1..18, 9 per row; rows on the two 39mm
  ;;   edges at y=+/-10.5000; pitch 3.9289mm (drawing 3.93+-0.1);
  ;;   outer pad centre 3.7844mm from the 39mm end (drawing 3.78+-0.1);
  ;;   closure 2*3.7844 + 8*3.9289 = 39.0000mm = module length 39.00.
  ;; VERIFIED land size - DERIVED from the operator-supplied datum:
  ;;   pad LAND SIZE 1.3 x 1.3 mm
  ;;     castellation HALF-HOLE diameter D = 0.8 +/- 0.1 mm, the
  ;;       operator's reading of the vendor drawing (datasheet s9 p8,
  ;;       a raster with no text layer). The module presents D of
  ;;       copper along the edge and penetrates only D/2 inward.
  ;;     RULE: land = the castellation aperture grown by a uniform
  ;;       0.25 mm solder-fillet margin on EVERY side.
  ;;       x: D + 2*0.25 = 1.3 mm; gap to the next land = 3.9289 - 1.3 = 2.6289 mm
  ;;       y: D + 2*0.25 = 1.3 mm, symmetric about the pad centre (pinned
  ;;          on the module edge, y=+/-10.5, and NOT moved): inward 0.65 >= D/2 = 0.4 mm;
  ;;          outward 0.65 = the hand-solder iron's access, never smaller than
  ;;          the inward half. F33-LANDPATTERN-VERIFICATION.md s11.
  ;; NOT verified (do not read this as verified):
